  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Saw_Teong_Hin">
    <rdfs:label>Saw Teong Hin</rdfs:label>
    <ns1:abstract>Saw Teong Hin (Chinese: 蘇倧興; Pe̍h-ōe-jī: So͘ Tiong-hèng) is a Malaysian film director, best known for directing the Malay language epic fantasy film Puteri Gunung Ledang and You Mean the World to Me, the first Malaysian film filmed entirely in Hokkien.</ns1:abstract>
