    <rdfs:label>Alcoa Theatre</rdfs:label>
    <ns1:runtime rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#double">1500.0</ns1:runtime>
    <ns1:abstract>Alcoa Theatre is a half-hour American anthology series telecast on NBC at 9:30 pm on Monday nights from September 30, 1957 to May 23, 1960. The program also aired under the title Turn of Fate. Alcoa Theatre was syndicated together with Goodyear Theatre as Award Theatre. In 1955, The Alcoa Hour premiered in a one-hour format aired on Sunday nights, but it was reduced to 30 minutes, retitled Alcoa Theatre, and moved to Monday evening in 1957. The show employed an alternating rotating company of actors: David Niven, Robert Ryan, Jane Powell, Jack Lemmon and Charles Boyer. Each appeared in dramatic and light comedic roles through the first season.</ns1:abstract>
    <ns1:starring rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Jane_Powell"/>
