  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Camp_Wilder">
    <ns1:director rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Arlene_Sanford"/>
    <ns1:rating>N/A</ns1:rating>
    <ns1:abstract>Camp Wilder is an American television sitcom which aired on ABC from September 18, 1992 until February 26, 1993. The premise centered on a young woman who opens up her home to the friends of her younger siblings, who sought it as judgment-free "hangout", and who regularly went to her for advice. The series was created by Matthew Carlson, and produced by a.k.a. Productions in association with Capital Cities Entertainment. The show aired as a part of ABC's TGIF lineup, but was cancelled after 19 episodes due to low ratings. A twentieth episode was produced, but was never aired in the United States. Camp Wilder was also shown in the UK, Spain and Germany.</ns1:abstract>
    <ns1:genre>http://dbpedia.org/resource/Sitcom</ns1:genre>
    <ns1:starring rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Mary_Page_Keller"/>
    <ns1:starring rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Meghann_Haldeman"/>
    <ns1:starring rdf:resource="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Margaret_Langrick"/>
