  <rdf:Description rdf:about="http://dbpedia.org/resource/Birgitta_Valberg">
    <ns1:abstract>Birgitta Valberg (16 December 1916 – 29 March 2014) was a Swedish actress. She was best known for her work in several Ingmar Bergman films made over a 30-year period, including the Bergman produced Paradise Place (1977). For her role in this film, which was directed by Gunnel Lindblom, another member of Bergman's repertory company, she won the award for Best Actress at the 13th Guldbagge Awards. She trained at the Royal Dramatic Training Academy.</ns1:abstract>
